==English==
[[File:Kintetsu Bus 001 JPN.jpg|thumb|A bus (motor vehicle).]]
[[File:Arriva_London_North_bus_DW433_(LJ11_AEA),_6_May_2013.jpg|thumb|A London [[double-decker bus]].]]
{{wp}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=omnibus|:clip|omnibus|tree=1}}
{{clipping|en|omnibus}}. Superseded earlier {{m|en|'bus}}, where the apostrophe indicated a clipping. The shift in spelling likely reflects the fact that modern speakers no longer perceive this term as a clipping. The electrical sense is derived from figurative application of the automotive sense.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/bʌs/}}, {{enPR|bŭs}}
** {{IPA|en|/bʊs/|a=Northern England,Ireland}}
** {{IPA|en|/bʌs/|a=Scotland}}
** {{IPA|en|/bɐs/|a=AU,NZ,Mid-Atlantic,Philippines}}
** {{IPA|en|/bɔs/|a=[[w:Inland Northern American English#Northern Cities Vowel Shift|Northern Cities Vowel Shift]],Ireland}}
** {{IPA|en|/bʊz/|a=[[w:Birmingham|Birmingham]], [[w:Black Country|Black Country]]}}
* {{audio|en|en-Buss.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-bus.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|Buss|buss}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌs|s=1}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|+|busses}}

# {{lb|en|automotive}} A [[motor]] [[vehicle]] for [[transport]]ing large numbers of [[people]] along [[road]]s.
#: {{co|en|I'm on the '''bus'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I can't read on the '''bus''' because I get sick.}}
#: {{syn|en|autobus|coach|loser cruiser|motorbus|motorcoach|omnibus|Shillibeer<ll:obsolete>}}
#: {{hypo|en|booze bus|commuter bus|school bus|short bus}}
## {{lb|en|chiefly|US|Canada}} A [[coach]], a bus used for long travels.
# {{lb|en|UK|dated}} Any motorized vehicle, such as a motorbike or car.
# {{lb|en|electronics}} An [[electrical]] [[conductor]] or [[interface]] serving as a [[common]] [[connection]] for two or more [[circuit]]s or [[component]]s.
#: {{syn|en|busbar|digit trunk|electrical bus}}
#: {{hypo|en|data bus}}
# Part of a [[MIRV]] [[missile]], having [[on-board]] [[motor]]s used to deliver the [[warhead]] to a [[target]].
# {{lb|en|medical industry|slang}} An [[ambulance]].
# {{lb|en|military slang|1910s–1940s}} An [[aeroplane]].<ref>{{R:en:Lighter:1972|page=26}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|networking}} A [[network topology]] with each computer connected to a single [[cable]].

