{{see translation subpage|Verb}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ety|en|id=busboy|:bf|busboy}}
{{back-formation|en|busboy}}.<ref>{{R:Garner's|edition=5th|pos=''n.'' & ''v.t.''|noformat=1|page=166|column=2|passage=The verb ''bus'', as a {{smallcaps|back-formation}} from ''busboy'', has the additional meanings ‘to work as a busboy or busgirl’ and ‘to clear dishes from (a table).’|nodot=1}}</ref>

====Verb====
{{en-verb|buses|busing|bused|pres_3sg2=busses|pres_ptc2=bussing|past2=bussed}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|US|food service}} To [[clear]] meal [[remains]] from.
#: {{ux|en|He '''bussed''' tables as the restaurant emptied out.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|US|food service}} To work at clearing the remains of meals from tables or counters; to work as a [[busboy]].
#: {{ux|en|He’s been '''bussing''' for minimum wage.}}

